  "design": {
    "brief": {
      "purpose": "ride",
      "hierarchy": "landmark",
      "style": "midway",
      "narrative": "A red-and-white striped drum forty-two courses tall at the Midway's east end, with a blue-ice helix wound one and three-quarter turns round the outside of it. A rider queues in the west yard, climbs two courses onto the boarding deck and steps off it into a trough of water whose far end is a three-by-three soul-sand bubble column; the column carries them twenty-five courses up the inside of the drum to a floor under a band of windows that looks west to the wheel and east to Prismworks; they walk out of the top door onto the chute and slide down and round the tower to a packed-ice run-out in the east yard, which is the opposite side from the queue. A thirteen-wide walk off the Prize Point, an arch that names the ride, and a planted terrace either side of it are the whole of the forecourt - no building at all.\n"
    },
